d retry with backoff to `WeatherClient.get` in `weather.py`. On a 503 it makes up to 3 attempts in total, waiting `backoff * 2**attempt` between them (0.5s, then 1.0s by default). I checked it against a real local HTTP server and all four cases behaved as expected.\n\n**Behaviour:**\n- **503:** retried. If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised to the caller.\n- **Any other HTTP error:** raised straight away with no retry.\n- **Network errors and timeouts:** not retried, since you only asked for 503.\n\n**New constructor options:**\n- **`backoff`** (default 0.5): the starting delay in seconds.\n- **`sleep`** (default `time.sleep`): lets tests skip the real waiting.\n\n**What the local server test showed:**\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests | Waits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 200 straight away | JSON returned | 1 | none |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | JSON returned | 3 | 0.5, 1.0 |\n| 503 three times | 503 error raised | 3 | 0.5, 1.0 |\n| 500 | 500 error raised | 1 | none |\n\nThis was a one-off script; the repo has no test suite, so I didn't add a test file.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 105619, "requests_cache_write": 73656, "requests_cost_usd": 0.4245518, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1755, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial9", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 76, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:48:10.165561+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 21.871, "t_checker_s": 5.389, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_bas